  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="features">
    <h2 id="features">Built around Apple system experiences.</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">Gus connects to a Jellyfin server you provide, then uses native Apple frameworks for browsing, playback, downloads, accessibility, and platform navigation.</p>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <article class="feature">
        <h3>Connect to your server</h3>
        <p>Sign in to your own Jellyfin server, browse libraries, search media, and open item details from an Apple-native SwiftUI interface.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <h3>System playback</h3>
        <p>Video playback is built on AVKit with system controls. Compatible files play at original quality — HDR and surround sound preserved where your device supports them — with a streaming-quality setting for constrained networks. Audio uses Now Playing and AirPlay where the platform supports them.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <h3>Downloads where supported</h3>
        <p>iPhone, iPad, Mac, and Apple Vision Pro can save compatible media from your server for local playback. Apple TV streams only.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <h3>Apple TV streaming</h3>
        <p>The tvOS experience follows Apple TV focus, remote, and playback conventions for living-room use.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <h3>visionOS Cinema</h3>
        <p>Apple Vision Pro support includes a native app experience and a Gus Cinema path for immersive playback scenarios.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="feature">
        <h3>Privacy by design</h3>
        <p>The app does not operate a developer backend and does not collect analytics, tracking data, server URLs, media metadata, or credentials for the developer.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

